# Navigation transitions

- Every **`Stack`** in `src/app/**/_layout.tsx` must set **`screenOptions.animation`** explicitly (`slide_from_right` by default, or per-screen overrides). Never leave the root navigator without an explicit animation so nested pushes feel consistent project-wide.
- **Default choice in this repo:** use **`slide_from_right`** for root and nested stacks so screens stay fully opaque during transitions. **`fade`** can read as a persistent dimmed veil on some Android / Fabric builds; reserve **`fade`** only for intentional cross-fades (override per-screen).
- Set **`contentStyle`** to the themed background alongside animation so fades do not flash a wrong backdrop.
- If a screen truly must appear without motion (e.g. splash), override that screen via `<Stack.Screen name="..." options={{ animation: 'none' }} />` locally — do not remove animation from the whole stack by default.

```tsx
const colors = useThemeColors();

return (
  <Stack
    screenOptions={{
      headerShown: false,
      contentStyle: { backgroundColor: colors.background },
      animation: 'slide_from_right',
    }}
  />
);
```

When adding nested layouts, match sibling stacks so auth, onboarding, and home transitions feel cohesive.
